[Music]  my mom is the bomb we're more like best  friends we're just always goofing off we  love to hang out together like that's my  girl my mom as a person she's vivacious  she just steps into a room and the whole  world lights up she's one of the most  important people in my life my mom is  the strongest person I know she's a  single mom raised my sister and I and  has been there through a lot of hard  times for both my sister and I  especially recently I used to just be  next to her when she would be washing  the dishes and that would be like my  favorite time because I just get to talk  and tell her all the gossip in school  and talk about nothing really but she  was always there we just have a good  time together we're always laughing I  can't even remember a time where I've  actually gotten to an argument with her  or been mad at her we just don't we  don't have a relationship like that I  can tell her absolutely anything she has  been my best friend since day one we are  really close we talk every day if I  don't hear from my mom on a day or two  days it's like a weird thing  she always pushed me my hardest but she  also had such a soft spot for me my mom  called me one day when I was at work and  said don't freak out I'm sure it's no  big deal but I have a lump in my neck so  the first time was breast cancer the  second time was ovarian and third time  was skin so it's been a long road I  think being a single mom it's that much  harder to bring bad news to your  children and it kind of scared them for  the future there were no signs of  anything when she had the mammogram  something just didn't feel normal  she flew to Taiwan and we heard from our  mom and her dad over the telephone that  she had cervical cancer she couldn't  bring herself to say anything just  hi honey like what like no it's like  she's my mom  you know that cancer happens to any and  everybody but when it happens to you  it's like oh my god and then to happen  to my mother my best friends it was  something I wasn't ready for and I know  she wasn't ready for either don't really  remember how I felt I just remember  being kind of like what do we do now my  first reaction though was I'm going home  I need to drop everything and go help  her in her time of need  just watching her go through it was very  emotional because I felt like I couldn't  do anything for her everything happens  for a reason which is a big mantra in my  family I don't know how much you want me  to go into this I was only because I  just got diagnosed with breast cancer  [Music]  so definitely learned a lot from this  they don't know that I would have  handled all this as well if I hadn't had  her about my side for every appointment  every surgery every doctor's visit and  test result oh I wasn't sure if I was  gonna even like talk about myself today  can you roll with the punches my sister  my dad and I were all in the same room  when it happened it was actually more  peaceful than I thought it would be I  had 18 amazing years with my mom I feel  like sometimes when things go well and  something has gotta be like it for me  it's probably her so I just wanted her  to know that I'm with you I can't feel  the pain that you're going through but  I'm with you in June my mom will be  three years breast cancer free she's  stronger mentally now because of it and  physically my mom is doing really well  she's actually healthier now than she  was before  cancer know that you're not alone in  this process unfortunately there are a  lot of people who are battling with  cancer just know that you're stronger  than what you think you are  support sisters are everything you know  people think it's cliche to say like let  me know if I couldn't do anything  there's really nothing necessarily you  can do except to show your support and  ensure that you're there even for  something as simple as a phone call or  you know coffee just to let them know  that they have you know shoulder to lean  on is really helpful I want to say  something like easy like time will help  but I don't know if  has helped that much if someone's going  through this right now I hope they know  that the pain that they feel is it'll  come in waves you know and like you just  have to ride the wave sometimes I guess  mom I just want to say that I love you  and I'm proud of you the journey still  continues but you got this you are the  strongest most badass person and I'm so  proud to be your daughter thank you for  being everything you've taught me so  much about life and persevering and  especially now I don't know where I'd be  without you I would really want her to  know that I'm okay for anyone battling  cancer or for anyone going through this  journey with someone there are a lot of  resources out there annual walks dancing  events like dancing with the survivors  and then there's also like message  boards and stuff like that people you  can talk to when you feel like you don't  have the answers you feel like you're  just alone battling something that you  didn't ask for so there's always people  you can talk to there's always ways that  you can help others you just have to go  to google and search it out  you  [Music]

